-- id: exp6875-text-anchored-relation-asp-fixture
-  title: Text-anchored relation and bounded ASP atom fixture
-  track: infrastructure
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 300
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.602
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6875_text_anchored_relation_asp_fixture.json
-  gated_on:
-    - upstream: exp6874-v602-evidence-substrate-manifest-contract
-      artifact_field: v602_evidence_contract_ready_score
-      op: '=='
-      value: 1
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Enoki represents a claim and its text location with one anchored relational fact. Carnot already
-    has a bounded ASP energy compiler with independent solver parity in Exp6274. Exp6275 exercised
-    natural-language ASP tasks but ended partial because required test exits failed. This task builds
-    a smaller source-grounded relation-to-atom fixture. It performs no model inference.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/research-references.md, V602 Planner Refresh
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6274_asp_energy_semantic_compiler.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6275_flagship_asp_constraint_verification_benchmark.json
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/asp_energy_semantic_compiler.py
-    - {project_root}/tests/python/test_asp_energy_semantic_compiler_6274.py
-    - {project_root}/tests/python/test_experiment_6275_flagship_asp_constraint_verification_benchmark.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-verification/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-store/spec.md
-
-    TASK:
-    Define a versioned text-anchored relation record and an exact map to the supported bounded ASP
-    subset. Build frozen calibration and sealed-held fixtures over graph coloring, scheduling,
-    non-monotonic defaults, contradictions, and cardinality constraints. Prove relation-to-atom and
-    atom-to-energy parity against the independent solver.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require v602_evidence_contract_ready_score=1, Exp6274 semantic parity, a
-       working independent ASP solver, and the checked-in Exp6274 fixture manifest. On failure,
-       write complete_blocked_text_anchored_relation_asp_fixture with gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-CONSTRAINT-6875 and tests first. Cover invalid spans, overlapping spans, unknown
-       entities, unsupported predicates, duplicate relations, negation, cardinality, default
-       negation, atom collisions, unsupported ASP syntax, sidecar leakage, and solver disagreement.
-    2. Define relation_record_v1 with fixture_id, source_text, source_span, subject, predicate,
-       object, polarity, evidence_span, normalized_tuple, asp_atom, and provenance hash.
-    3. Use a closed predicate and entity vocabulary derived only from the supported Exp6274 subset.
-       Reject free-form predicates, missing evidence, and tuples that cannot map injectively.
-    4. Build at least 120 fixtures with valid, invalid, omitted, contradictory, and abstain cases.
-       Cover all five families and keep difficulty and relation count balanced.
-    5. Freeze group-disjoint calibration and held splits. Put exact labels, ASP programs, answer
-       sets, and solver receipts in sealed sidecars that the future model prompt builder cannot read.
-    6. Compile every accepted relation set with the bounded compiler. Require zero-energy states to
-       equal the independent solver answer sets. Preserve local rule-violation receipts.
-    7. Add prompt nonexposure tests for ASP syntax, exact answers, labels, solver receipts, hashes,
-       and hidden sidecar fields.
-    8. Set relation_fact_fixture_ready_score=1 only when schema validation, span checks, injective
-       mapping, family floors, split isolation, sidecar sealing, and exact parity all pass.
-    9. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, independent solver parity, adversarial
-       verification, artifact-convention audit, verdict-row consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
-    10. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one principle per required field and every
-       gate field; preconditions_checked; inference_substrate
-       (deterministic_exact_relation_asp_fixture_no_llm); duration_s; source_artifact_hashes;
-       relation_schema_version; closed_vocabulary_manifest; rows (one fixture and relation);
-       fixture_family_counts; calibration_group_manifest; sealed_held_group_manifest;
-       split_overlap_count (zero); relation_to_atom_rows; atom_collision_rows; unsupported_rows;
-       solver_parity_rows; rule_violation_receipts; prompt_nonexposure_results;
-       independent_solver_receipts; random_seed; reproducibility_checksum;
-       relation_fact_fixture_ready_score (exact field consumed by Exp6876); gate_check_summary with
-       failed check, expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict;
-       verifier_is_oracle (true); verdict_class (circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified |
-       partial; never positive); honest_verdict (terminal and prefixed complete_).
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6875_text_anchored_relation_asp_fixture.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
-  prior_failures:
-    - experiment_id: exp6275-flagship-asp-constraint-verification-benchmark
-      verdict: 'complete_partial: test_exit_codes'
-      addressed_by: 'This task narrows the deliverable to a deterministic relation-to-atom fixture, reuses the already-qualified Exp6274 compiler, and requires task-owned focused test exits before readiness.'
-      retire_if_same_verdict: true
